      "message": "Nit: this says the shared isolate\u0027s `call` returns a future, but 0026 #2 makes `call` always synchronous and `call_async` always the future.\n\nWhat shows it: `docs/adr/0008-threading-model.md:32` says a `SharedIsolate` is one \"whose `call` returns a `\u0027static + Send` future\", while 0026 item 2 states \"`call` is always synchronous and `call_async` always the future, on the owned `Isolate` and on `SharedIsolate`\", and item 4 gives the shared isolate synchronous `with` and `call` plus `Call::run()`, with the future coming from `call_async` or from the `Call` itself via `IntoFuture`.\n\nFix: say \"whose `call_async` returns a `\u0027static + Send` future\" (or \"whose `Call` is a `\u0027static + Send` future\").",
